44	/**
45	 * Advances the duel by one 60 Hz frame (order of operations in docs/duel.md):
46	 *
47	 * 1. read both inputs (opposite directions cancel; newly pressed buttons enter the 4-frame buffer);
48	 * 2. detect every hit, block and grab of the frame against the start-of-frame state of both fighters;
49	 * 3. settle same-frame interactions (throw against throw breaks both; a strike that hits or is blocked beats a throw);
50	 * 4. apply all results together, damage and stamina from start-of-frame values; fighters not struck advance their
51	 *    action (a light or heavy may still become the throw inside the chord window) or start a new one from their input;
52	 * 5. move, apply gravity, keep fighters inside the walls and apart;
53	 * 6. regenerate stamina, then decide KO, timeout and overtime from both fighters' health.
54	 *
55	 * Neither fighter is processed "first": every decision for one fighter reads only the start-of-frame state and the
56	 * frame's inputs. The input state is never mutated. A finished duel only advances its frame counter.
